								Blarg<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=251"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg2461#msg2461"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg2461#msg2461">Re:And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #65 on:</b> October 26, 2003, 10:27:44 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							To clear some stuff up about Verzi.<br /><br />Yes we are a European guild, and we are casual at raiding. only do it 4-5 times a week or so. Which puts us on CET time.<br /><br />We have killed everything in Ssra except Cursed and Emperor, and are currently working on Emperor keys.<br /><br />We have killed all PoP tier 1 mobs.<br />Did PoV dragon on first attempt with 38 people (including 2 boxed clerics etc) and have done Caprin Cycle in CoD a few times. We have done the first 2 trials in HoH, and one test run against the Dragon on 3rd trial with 29 people.<br /><br />Currently waiting on Agnarr and HoH trial 3 to be up on our raid time, and also working on Bertox ring.<br /><br />Does that place us above UoP? Frankly I do not know, it depends on if you place Tier 2 boss mobs above VT level. And I dont really care, to tell the truth <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/smiley1.gif" alt="Smiley" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
